{"tool_name":"ccd2","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"ccd2","home":"https://ccd.rhpc.nki.nl","license":"Other","summary":"Crystallization Construct Designer 2 (CCD2) a tool to design protein truncation constructs for recombinant expression","addition_date":"2021-12-15T18:02:27.626117Z","last_update_date":"2021-12-15T18:02:27.630937Z","tool_type":["Desktop application","Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access (with restrictions)","biotools_curie":"biotools:ccd2","cost":"Free of charge (with restrictions)","credit":[{"email":"a.murachelli@nki.nl","name":"Andrea Giovanni Murachelli","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2968-8972","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"a.perrakis@nki.nl","name":"Anastassis Perrakis","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1151-6227","typeEntity":"Person"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://ccd.rhpc.nki.nl/tutorial"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Fold recognition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0303"},{"term":"PCR primer design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0308"},{"term":"Phylogenetic inference","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0323"},{"term":"Protein secondary structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0267"},{"term":"Sequence trimming","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3192"}]}],"name":"CCD2","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1107/S2059798321005891","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021 International Union of Crystallography. All rights reserved.Studying the function or structure of proteins usually requires the generation of many protein-truncation constructs for recombinant expression, which is a tedious and error-prone job. CCD 2 is a software tool designed to facilitate and automate this task. CCD 2 helps scientists by aggregating the information necessary to design protein-expression constructs. This information includes sequence conservation, secondary structure prediction, domain(s) and disorder detection, post-translational modifications and information on similar (domain) structures that are available in the Protein Data Bank. CCD 2 then allows users to easily choose the boundaries for protein constructs and automatically generates the primers necessary for construct amplification by polymerase chain reaction. Finally, CCD 2 provides a quick analysis of the properties of the chosen constructs, together with their DNA vector maps for bookkeeping. The features of CCD 2 are discussed step by step, showing that it can be a useful tool for laboratories that engage in recombinant protein production for any type of experiment, and in particular for structural biology studies.","authors":[{"name":"Damaskos G."},{"name":"Murachelli A.G."},{"name":"Perrakis A."}],"date":"2021-08-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Acta Crystallographica Section D: Structural Biology","title":"CCD 2: Design constructs for protein expression, the easy way"},"pmcid":"PMC8329859","pmid":"34342272"}],"topic":[{"term":"Model organisms","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0621"},{"term":"Probes and primers","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0632"},{"term":"Protein modifications","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0601"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"},{"term":"Transcription factors and regulatory sites","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0749"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"CCD2","home":"https://bio.tools/ccd2","license":"Other","summary":"Crystallization Construct Designer 2 (CCD2) a tool to design protein truncation constructs for recombinant expression","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:ccd2/app/ccd.rhpc.nki.nl","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true,"repositor